/-!
# The weight filtration of a polynomial ring and its Rees algebra

Give the variable `X i` of `MvPolynomial σ R` the weight `w i ∈ ℕ`, so that the monomial `X^u`
has weight `Finsupp.weight w u`. The polynomials all of whose monomials have weight at most `n`
form the `n`-th step `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightFiltration R w n` of an increasing, exhaustive,
multiplicative filtration, a native `IsRingFiltration` whose lower stages
`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightFiltrationLT R w n` are the polynomials whose monomials have weight
less than `n`. Each step is the sum of the step below it and of the weighted homogeneous
polynomials of weight `n`, and these two pieces are independent. So the `n`-th associated graded
piece is identified with the weighted homogeneous polynomials of weight `n`, and the polynomial
ring with its weight grading plays the role of the associated graded ring.

The Rees algebra `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightReesAlgebra R w` of this filtration is the
subalgebra of `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` of polynomials whose coefficient of `tⁿ` lies in the `n`-th
step: it is `TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra` of the filtration. It is again a polynomial ring, with the
Rees parameter `t` as one of its variables: substituting `X i * t ^ w i` for `X i` and fixing `t`
gives an isomorphism `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightReesEquiv R w` from `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` onto
the Rees algebra. The monomial `X^v tᵏ` goes to `X^v t^(k + weight w v)`, and these are exactly
the monomials of the Rees algebra, each reached once. The fibre of the Rees algebra at `t = 1`
corresponds to setting `t = 1`. Its fibre at `t = 0` is the polynomial ring with its weight
grading: the symbol map `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightReesSymbol R w` sends `b tⁿ`, for `b` of
weight at most `n`, to the weighted homogeneous component of weight `n` of `b`, and its kernel is
generated by `t`. Conversely, for `p` of weight at most `n`, the preimage of `p tⁿ` is the
homogenization `MvPolynomial.weightHomogenization R w n p = ∑ p_v X^v t^(n - weight w v)`,
whose value at `t = 1` is `p` and whose value at `t = 0` is the weighted homogeneous component of
weight `n` of `p`.

A family `c i` of polynomials of weights at most `d i` degenerates, through the substitution
`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightReesAeval c d` of `c i * t ^ d i` for the variables `Y i`, to the
family of their weighted homogeneous components of weight `d i`, their *initial forms*: on the
symbols of the Rees algebra, substituting the `c i` becomes substituting their initial forms.

This is the ambient family for degenerating polynomial ideals and subalgebras to their weight
initial forms: they inherit the filtration, and their Rees algebras sit inside this one.

## Main definitions

All declarations live in the namespace `TauCeti.MvPolynomial`, except the lemmas about the image
of a polynomial `f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[t]`, which live in the root namespace `Polynomial` so
that dot notation `f.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom` applies, and the homogenization
`weightHomogenization` with its lemmas not involving the weight filtration, which act on a
polynomial `p : MvPolynomial σ R` and so live in the root namespace `MvPolynomial`.

* `weightFiltration R w n`, `weightFiltrationLT R w n`: the steps of weight at most `n` and less
  than `n`.
* `weightReesAlgebra R w`: the Rees algebra of the weight filtration.
* `weightReesHom R w`: the injective substitution `X i ↦ X i * t ^ w i`, `t ↦ t`, which is
  `weightReesAeval X w`.
* `weightReesEquiv R w`: the isomorphism from `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` onto the Rees algebra.
* `weightReesSymbol R w`: the symbol map from the Rees algebra onto the associated graded ring
  `MvPolynomial σ R`.
* `weightHomogenization R w n`: the homogenization `X^v ↦ X^v t^(n - weight w v)` in degree `n`.
* `weightReesAeval c d`: the substitution `Y i ↦ c i * t ^ d i`, `t ↦ t`, from
  `(MvPolynomial ι R)[t]` to `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]`.

## Main results

* `weightFiltration.instIsRingFiltration`: the weight filtration is a ring filtration.
* `iSup_weightFiltration`: it is exhaustive.
* `weightFiltrationLT_sup_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule`,
  `disjoint_weightFiltrationLT_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule`: the `n`-th step is the independent
  sum of the lower stage and of the weighted homogeneous polynomials of weight `n`.
* `Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom`, `range_weightReesHom`: the coefficient of `X^v tⁿ` in
  the image of `f` is that of `X^v t^(n - weight w v)` in `f` when `weight w v ≤ n`, and `0`
  otherwise, and the image is the Rees algebra.
* `Polynomial.evalOne_weightReesEquiv`: the fibre at `t = 1` is evaluation at `t = 1`.
* `weightReesSymbol_monomial`, `ker_weightReesSymbol`: the symbol of `b tⁿ` is the weighted
  homogeneous component of weight `n` of `b`, and the kernel of the symbol map is generated by the
  Rees parameter.
* `weightReesHom_weightHomogenization`, `weightHomogenization_mul`: for `p` of weight at most `n`,
  `weightReesHom` sends the homogenization of `p` in degree `n` to `p tⁿ`, and homogenization is
  multiplicative on the steps of the filtration.
* `coeff_zero_weightHomogenization_sub`: for `r` weighted homogeneous of weight `n` and `Q` of
  weight less than `n`, the homogenization of `r - Q` in degree `n` reduces to `r` at `t = 0`.
* `weightReesAeval_mem_weightReesAlgebra`, `aeval_mem_weightFiltration`: if each `c i` has weight
  at most `d i`, then `weightReesAeval c d` takes values in the Rees algebra, and substituting the
  `c i` into a polynomial of weight at most `n` for the weights `d` gives a polynomial of weight at
  most `n`.
* `weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval_of_mem_weightFiltration`: if moreover `g i` is the
  component of weight `d i` of `c i`, the component of weight `n` of the substitution is the
  substitution of the `g i` into the component of weight `n`.

## References

* D. Eisenbud, *Commutative Algebra with a View Toward Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 150, §6.5 and
  §15.8 (Rees algebras of filtrations and flat degenerations to initial ideals).
* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 1.
-/

public section

open scoped Polynomial

namespace TauCeti.MvPolynomial

open _root_.MvPolynomial

variable {σ R : Type*} [CommSemiring R]

section Filtration

variable (R) (w : σ → ℕ)

/-- The `n`-th step of the weight filtration of `MvPolynomial σ R` for the weights `w`: the
polynomials all of whose monomials have weight at most `n`. -/
noncomputable def weightFiltration (n : ℕ) : Submodule R (MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  restrictSupport R {u | Finsupp.weight w u ≤ n}

/-- The lower stage below the `n`-th step of the weight filtration: the polynomials all of whose
monomials have weight less than `n`. -/
noncomputable def weightFiltrationLT (n : ℕ) : Submodule R (MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  restrictSupport R {u | Finsupp.weight w u < n}

variable {R w}

theorem mem_weightFiltration_iff {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    p ∈ weightFiltration R w n ↔ ∀ u ∈ p.support, Finsupp.weight w u ≤ n :=
  mem_restrictSupport_iff R

theorem mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    p ∈ weightFiltrationLT R w n ↔ ∀ u ∈ p.support, Finsupp.weight w u < n :=
  mem_restrictSupport_iff R

/-- A polynomial lies in the `n`-th step of the weight filtration exactly when its weighted total
degree is at most `n`. -/
theorem mem_weightFiltration_iff_weightedTotalDegree_le {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    p ∈ weightFiltration R w n ↔ weightedTotalDegree w p ≤ n := by
  rw [mem_weightFiltration_iff, weightedTotalDegree, Finset.sup_le_iff]

@[simp]
theorem monomial_mem_weightFiltration_iff {n : ℕ} {u : σ →₀ ℕ} {r : R} :
    monomial u r ∈ weightFiltration R w n ↔ Finsupp.weight w u ≤ n ∨ r = 0 :=
  monomial_mem_restrictSupport R

@[simp]
theorem monomial_mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff {n : ℕ} {u : σ →₀ ℕ} {r : R} :
    monomial u r ∈ weightFiltrationLT R w n ↔ Finsupp.weight w u < n ∨ r = 0 :=
  monomial_mem_restrictSupport R

theorem C_mem_weightFiltration (r : R) (n : ℕ) : C r ∈ weightFiltration R w n := by
  rw [C_apply, monomial_mem_weightFiltration_iff, map_zero]
  exact Or.inl n.zero_le

theorem X_mem_weightFiltration (i : σ) :
    (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ∈ weightFiltration R w (w i) := by
  simp [X, Finsupp.weight_single]

theorem weightFiltration_mono : Monotone (weightFiltration R w) :=
  fun _ _ h ↦ restrictSupport_mono R fun _ hu ↦ le_trans hu h

theorem weightFiltrationLT_le_weightFiltration (n : ℕ) :
    weightFiltrationLT R w n ≤ weightFiltration R w n :=
  restrictSupport_mono R (Set.ofPred_subset_ofPred.mpr fun _ ↦ le_of_lt)

@[simp]
theorem weightFiltrationLT_zero : weightFiltrationLT R w 0 = ⊥ := by
  rw [Submodule.eq_bot_iff]
  intro p hp
  rw [← support_eq_empty, Finset.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem]
  exact fun u hu ↦ Nat.not_lt_zero _ (mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.mp hp u hu)

@[simp]
theorem weightFiltrationLT_succ (n : ℕ) :
    weightFiltrationLT R w (n + 1) = weightFiltration R w n := by
  simp [weightFiltrationLT, weightFiltration]

/-- Every polynomial lies in some step of the weight filtration. -/
theorem iSup_weightFiltration : ⨆ n, weightFiltration R w n = ⊤ := by
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun p _ ↦ Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (weightedTotalDegree w p) ?_
  exact mem_weightFiltration_iff_weightedTotalDegree_le.mpr le_rfl

namespace weightFiltration

instance instGradedMonoid : SetLike.GradedMonoid (weightFiltration R w) where
  one_mem := by simpa using C_mem_weightFiltration (w := w) (1 : R) 0
  mul_mem m n p q hp hq := by
    rw [weightFiltration] at hp hq ⊢
    refine restrictSupport_mono R ?_ (restrictSupport_add R _ _ ▸ Submodule.mul_mem_mul hp hq)
    rintro _ ⟨u, hu, v, hv, rfl⟩
    simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, map_add] at hu hv ⊢
    omega

/-- The weight filtration, with the polynomials of smaller weight as its lower stages, is a ring
filtration. -/
instance instIsRingFiltration :
    IsRingFiltration (weightFiltration R w) (weightFiltrationLT R w) where
  mono := weightFiltration_mono
  is_le {i j} h := by
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_lt h
    rw [weightFiltrationLT_succ]
    exact weightFiltration_mono (Nat.le_add_right i j)
  is_sup B j hB := by
    cases j with
    | zero => simp
    | succ j => simpa using hB j (Nat.lt_succ_self j)

end weightFiltration

/-- The `n`-th step of the weight filtration is spanned by its lower stage and the weighted
homogeneous polynomials of weight `n`. -/
theorem weightFiltrationLT_sup_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule (n : ℕ) :
    weightFiltrationLT R w n ⊔ weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n = weightFiltration R w n := by
  refine le_antisymm (sup_le (weightFiltrationLT_le_weightFiltration n) fun p hp ↦ ?_) ?_
  · rw [mem_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule] at hp
    exact mem_weightFiltration_iff.mpr fun u hu ↦ (hp (mem_support_iff.mp hu)).le
  · rw [weightFiltration, restrictSupport_eq_span, Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩
    replace hu : Finsupp.weight w u ≤ n := hu
    rcases hu.lt_or_eq with hu | hu
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_left (by simp [hu])
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_right (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial w u 1 hu)

/-- The lower stage below the `n`-th step of the weight filtration meets the weighted homogeneous
polynomials of weight `n` only in `0`. -/
theorem disjoint_weightFiltrationLT_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule (n : ℕ) :
    Disjoint (weightFiltrationLT R w n) (weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n) := by
  rw [Submodule.disjoint_def]
  intro p hlt hhom
  rw [← support_eq_empty, Finset.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem]
  intro u hu
  exact (mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.mp hlt u hu).ne
    ((mem_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n p).mp hhom (mem_support_iff.mp hu))

end Filtration

section ReesAeval

variable {ι : Type*}

variable (c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R) (d : ι → ℕ) in
/-- The Rees presentation map: the substitution `Y i ↦ c i * t ^ d i`, `t ↦ t`, from
`(MvPolynomial ι R)[t]` to `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]`. If each `c i` has weight at most `d i` for
weights `w`, its image lies in the Rees algebra of the weight filtration
(`weightReesAeval_mem_weightReesAlgebra`). Its image is the `R[t]`-algebra generated by the
`c i * t ^ d i`, which specializes to the subalgebra generated by the `c i` at `t = 1`. For
`c = X` it is `weightReesHom R d`, which is defined as this special case. -/
noncomputable def weightReesAeval : (MvPolynomial ι R)[X] →ₐ[R] (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] :=
  Polynomial.aevalTower (aeval fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (c i) * Polynomial.X ^ d i) Polynomial.X

variable {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R} {d : ι → ℕ}

@[simp]
theorem weightReesAeval_C {p : MvPolynomial ι R} :
    weightReesAeval c d (Polynomial.C p) =
      aeval (fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (c i) * Polynomial.X ^ d i) p :=
  Polynomial.aevalTower_C _ _ _

@[simp]
theorem weightReesAeval_X : weightReesAeval c d Polynomial.X = Polynomial.X :=
  Polynomial.aevalTower_X _ _

end ReesAeval

section Rees

variable (R) (w : σ → ℕ)

/-- The Rees algebra of the weight filtration: the polynomials `∑ bₙ tⁿ` over
`MvPolynomial σ R` such that every monomial of `bₙ` has weight at most `n`. -/
noncomputable abbrev weightReesAlgebra : Subalgebra R (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] :=
  TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra (weightFiltration R w)

/-- The constant `1` has weight at most one, so the Rees parameter `t` lies in the Rees
algebra. -/
theorem one_mem_weightFiltration_one : (1 : MvPolynomial σ R) ∈ weightFiltration R w 1 :=
  weightFiltration_mono zero_le_one SetLike.GradedOne.one_mem

/-- The endomorphism of `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` substituting `X i * t ^ w i` for `X i` and fixing
`t`; it is injective with image the Rees algebra. It is the case `c = X` of `weightReesAeval`. -/
noncomputable def weightReesHom : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] →ₐ[R] (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] :=
  weightReesAeval X w

variable {R w}

@[simp]
theorem weightReesHom_C {p : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    weightReesHom R w (Polynomial.C p) =
      aeval (fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (X i) * Polynomial.X ^ w i) p :=
  weightReesAeval_C

@[simp]
theorem weightReesHom_X : weightReesHom R w Polynomial.X = Polynomial.X :=
  weightReesAeval_X

/-- The coefficient of `X^v tⁿ` in the image of `f` under `weightReesHom` is the coefficient of
`X^v t^(n - weight w v)` in `f` when `weight w v ≤ n`, and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem _root_.Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom (f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) (n : ℕ)
    (v : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    ((weightReesHom R w f).coeff n).coeff v =
      if Finsupp.weight w v ≤ n then (f.coeff (n - Finsupp.weight w v)).coeff v else 0 := by
  classical
  induction f using Polynomial.induction_on' with
  | add f g hf hg =>
    simp only [map_add, Polynomial.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, Finsupp.add_apply, hf,
      hg]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  | monomial k p =>
    rw [← Polynomial.C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, map_mul, map_pow, weightReesHom_C, weightReesHom_X,
      Polynomial.coeff_mul_X_pow', Polynomial.coeff_C_mul_X_pow]
    simp only [coeff_aeval_C_X_mul_X_pow, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent,
      apply_ite (fun q : MvPolynomial σ R ↦ q.coeff v), AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_zero,
      Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
    split_ifs <;> first | rfl | omega

variable (R w) in
/-- Distinct monomials `X^v tᵏ` have distinct images `X^v t^(k + weight w v)`, so
`weightReesHom` is injective. -/
theorem weightReesHom_injective : Function.Injective (weightReesHom R w) := by
  intro f g h
  ext k v
  have hf := Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom (R := R) (w := w) f (k + Finsupp.weight w v) v
  have hg := Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom (R := R) (w := w) g (k + Finsupp.weight w v) v
  rw [ite_eq_left (Nat.le_add_left _ _), Nat.add_sub_cancel] at hf hg
  rw [← hf, ← hg, h]

/-- The image of `X^v tᵏ` under `weightReesHom` is `X^v t^(k + weight w v)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightReesHom_monomial_monomial (k : ℕ) (v : σ →₀ ℕ) (r : R) :
    weightReesHom R w (Polynomial.monomial k (monomial v r)) =
      Polynomial.monomial (k + Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v r) := by
  classical
  ext n u
  rw [Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom]
  simp only [Polynomial.coeff_monomial, coeff_monomial,
    apply_ite (fun q : MvPolynomial σ R ↦ q.coeff u), AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_zero,
    Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
  split_ifs <;> first | rfl | (subst_vars; omega)

variable (R w) in
/-- The image of `weightReesHom` is the Rees algebra of the weight filtration. -/
theorem range_weightReesHom : (weightReesHom R w).range = weightReesAlgebra R w := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ fun g hg ↦ ?_
  · intro g hg
    obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := ((weightReesHom R w).mem_range).mp hg
    refine TauCeti.mem_coeffSubalgebra_iff.mpr fun n ↦
      mem_weightFiltration_iff.mpr fun v hv ↦ ?_
    rw [mem_support_iff, Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom] at hv
    by_contra h
    exact hv (ite_eq_right h)
  -- Every monomial `X^v tⁿ` with `weight w v ≤ n` is the image of `X^v t^(n - weight w v)`.
  have key (n : ℕ) : weightFiltration R w n ≤ ((weightReesHom R w).range.toSubmodule.comap
      ((Polynomial.monomial n).restrictScalars R)) := by
    rw [weightFiltration, restrictSupport_eq_span, Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩
    replace hv : Finsupp.weight w v ≤ n := hv
    refine ((weightReesHom R w).mem_range).mpr
      ⟨Polynomial.monomial (n - Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v 1), ?_⟩
    rw [weightReesHom_monomial_monomial, Nat.sub_add_cancel hv, LinearMap.restrictScalars_apply]
  rw [← Polynomial.sum_monomial_eq g, Polynomial.sum_def]
  exact Subalgebra.sum_mem _ fun n _ ↦ key n (TauCeti.mem_coeffSubalgebra_iff.mp hg n)

variable (R w) in
/-- The Rees algebra of the weight filtration is isomorphic, as an `R`-algebra, to
`(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]`, a polynomial ring over `R` in the `X i` and `t`: the isomorphism sends
`X i` to `X i * t ^ w i` and fixes `t`. -/
noncomputable def weightReesEquiv : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] ≃ₐ[R] weightReesAlgebra R w :=
  (AlgEquiv.ofInjective _ (weightReesHom_injective R w)).trans
    (Subalgebra.equivOfEq _ _ (range_weightReesHom R w))

@[simp]
theorem _root_.Polynomial.coe_weightReesEquiv (f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) :
    (weightReesEquiv R w f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) = weightReesHom R w f := by
  simp [weightReesEquiv]

/-- The coefficient of `X^v tⁿ` in the image of `f` under `weightReesEquiv` is the coefficient of
`X^v t^(n - weight w v)` in `f` when `weight w v ≤ n`, and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem _root_.Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesEquiv (f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) (n : ℕ)
    (v : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    ((weightReesEquiv R w f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]).coeff n).coeff v =
      if Finsupp.weight w v ≤ n then (f.coeff (n - Finsupp.weight w v)).coeff v else 0 := by
  rw [Polynomial.coe_weightReesEquiv, Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom]

/-- The coefficient of `X^v tᵏ` in the preimage of `g` under `weightReesEquiv` is the coefficient
of `X^v t^(k + weight w v)` in `g`. -/
theorem coeff_coeff_weightReesEquiv_symm (g : weightReesAlgebra R w) (k : ℕ) (v : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    (((weightReesEquiv R w).symm g).coeff k).coeff v =
      ((g : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]).coeff (k + Finsupp.weight w v)).coeff v := by
  conv_rhs => rw [← (weightReesEquiv R w).apply_symm_apply g]
  rw [Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesEquiv, ite_eq_left (Nat.le_add_left _ _),
    Nat.add_sub_cancel]

/-- The isomorphism `weightReesEquiv` sends `t` to the Rees parameter. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightReesEquiv_X :
    weightReesEquiv R w Polynomial.X =
      TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w) :=
  Subtype.ext (by simp)

/-- The inverse of `weightReesEquiv` sends the Rees parameter to `t`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightReesEquiv_symm_X :
    (weightReesEquiv R w).symm (TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w)) =
      Polynomial.X :=
  (weightReesEquiv R w).symm_apply_eq.mpr weightReesEquiv_X.symm

/-- The fibre of the Rees algebra at `t = 1`: evaluating the image of `f` under `weightReesEquiv`
at `t = 1` is the evaluation of `f` at `t = 1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem _root_.Polynomial.evalOne_weightReesEquiv (f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) :
    TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.evalOne _ (weightReesEquiv R w f) = f.eval 1 := by
  have h : (TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.evalOne (weightFiltration R w)).comp
      (weightReesEquiv R w).toAlgHom =
        (Polynomial.aeval (1 : MvPolynomial σ R)).restrictScalars R := by
    refine Polynomial.algHom_ext' (MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i ↦ ?_) ?_ <;>
      simp [TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.evalOne_apply]
  simpa using congr($h f)

variable (R w) in
/-- The symbol map from the Rees algebra of the weight filtration to the associated graded ring,
the polynomial ring with its weight grading: `b tⁿ`, for `b` of weight at most `n`, goes to the
weighted homogeneous component of weight `n` of `b` (`weightReesSymbol_monomial`). -/
noncomputable def weightReesSymbol : weightReesAlgebra R w →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial σ R :=
  ((Polynomial.aeval (0 : MvPolynomial σ R)).restrictScalars R).comp
    (weightReesEquiv R w).symm.toAlgHom

@[simp]
theorem _root_.Polynomial.weightReesSymbol_weightReesEquiv (f : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) :
    weightReesSymbol R w (weightReesEquiv R w f) = f.coeff 0 := by
  simp [weightReesSymbol, Polynomial.coeff_zero_eq_aeval_zero]

/-- The coefficient of `X^v` in the symbol of `g` is the coefficient of `X^v t^(weight w v)` in
`g`. -/
theorem coeff_weightReesSymbol (g : weightReesAlgebra R w) (v : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    (weightReesSymbol R w g).coeff v =
      ((g : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]).coeff (Finsupp.weight w v)).coeff v := by
  obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := (weightReesEquiv R w).surjective g
  rw [Polynomial.weightReesSymbol_weightReesEquiv, Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesEquiv,
    ite_eq_left le_rfl, Nat.sub_self]

/-- The symbol of `b tⁿ`, for `b` of weight at most `n`, is the weighted homogeneous component of
weight `n` of `b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightReesSymbol_monomial {n : ℕ} {b : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hb : b ∈ weightFiltration R w n) :
    weightReesSymbol R w (TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.monomial _ n b hb) =
      weightedHomogeneousComponent w n b := by
  classical
  ext v
  rw [coeff_weightReesSymbol, TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.coe_monomial, Polynomial.coeff_monomial,
    coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent]
  split_ifs <;> first | rfl | (subst_vars; contradiction)

/-- The symbol map kills the Rees parameter. -/
@[simp]
theorem weightReesSymbol_X :
    weightReesSymbol R w (TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w)) = 0 := by
  rw [← weightReesEquiv_X, Polynomial.weightReesSymbol_weightReesEquiv, Polynomial.coeff_X_zero]

/-- Every polynomial is the symbol of an element of the Rees algebra, namely of its image under
`weightReesEquiv` as a constant in `t`. Together with `ker_weightReesSymbol`, this identifies the
fibre of the Rees algebra at `t = 0` with the polynomial ring. -/
theorem weightReesSymbol_surjective : Function.Surjective (weightReesSymbol R w) :=
  fun p ↦ ⟨weightReesEquiv R w (Polynomial.C p), by simp⟩

/-- The kernel of the symbol map is generated by the Rees parameter. -/
theorem ker_weightReesSymbol :
    RingHom.ker (weightReesSymbol R w) =
      Ideal.span {TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w)} := by
  ext g
  obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := (weightReesEquiv R w).surjective g
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, Polynomial.weightReesSymbol_weightReesEquiv, Ideal.mem_span_singleton,
    ← weightReesEquiv_X, map_dvd_iff, Polynomial.X_dvd_iff]

end Rees

section Homogenization

variable (R) (w : σ → ℕ)

/-- The homogenization in degree `n` for the weights `w`: the `R`-linear map
`MvPolynomial σ R → (MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` sending `X^v` to `X^v t^(n - weight w v)`. On the
`n`-th step of the weight filtration it inverts `weightReesHom` on `p tⁿ`
(`weightReesHom_weightHomogenization`), so `weightHomogenization R w n p` is the preimage of
`p tⁿ` under `weightReesEquiv`. -/
noncomputable def _root_.MvPolynomial.weightHomogenization (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial σ R →ₗ[R] (MvPolynomial σ R)[X] :=
  (basisMonomials σ R).constr R fun v ↦
    Polynomial.monomial (n - Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v 1)

variable {R w}

@[simp]
theorem _root_.MvPolynomial.weightHomogenization_monomial (n : ℕ) (v : σ →₀ ℕ) (r : R) :
    weightHomogenization R w n (monomial v r) =
      Polynomial.monomial (n - Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v r) := by
  have h1 : weightHomogenization R w n (monomial v 1) =
      Polynomial.monomial (n - Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v 1) := by
    simpa [weightHomogenization] using (basisMonomials σ R).constr_basis R
      (fun v ↦ Polynomial.monomial (n - Finsupp.weight w v) (monomial v (1 : R))) v
  have hr : monomial v r = r • monomial v (1 : R) := by rw [smul_monomial, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  rw [hr, map_smul, h1, Polynomial.smul_monomial]

/-- The coefficient of `X^v tᵏ` in the homogenization of `p` in degree `n` is the coefficient of
`X^v` in `p` when `n - weight w v = k`, and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem _root_.MvPolynomial.coeff_coeff_weightHomogenization (n k : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (v : σ →₀ ℕ) :
    ((weightHomogenization R w n p).coeff k).coeff v =
      if n - Finsupp.weight w v = k then p.coeff v else 0 := by
  classical
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on' with
  | monomial u r =>
    rcases eq_or_ne u v with rfl | huv
    · simp [Polynomial.coeff_monomial, apply_ite (fun q : MvPolynomial σ R ↦ q.coeff u)]
    · simp [Polynomial.coeff_monomial, apply_ite (fun q : MvPolynomial σ R ↦ q.coeff v),
        coeff_monomial, huv]
  | add p q hp hq =>
    simp only [map_add, Polynomial.coeff_add, AddMonoidAlgebra.coeff_add, Finsupp.add_apply, hp,
      hq]
    split_ifs <;> simp

/-- On the `n`-th step of the weight filtration, `weightReesHom` sends the homogenization of `p`
in degree `n` to `p tⁿ`. -/
theorem weightReesHom_weightHomogenization {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hp : p ∈ weightFiltration R w n) :
    weightReesHom R w (weightHomogenization R w n p) = Polynomial.monomial n p := by
  classical
  ext k v
  rw [Polynomial.coeff_coeff_weightReesHom, coeff_coeff_weightHomogenization,
    Polynomial.coeff_monomial]
  by_cases hv : p.coeff v = 0
  · split_ifs <;> simp [hv]
  · have := mem_weightFiltration_iff.mp hp v (mem_support_iff.mpr hv)
    split_ifs <;> first | rfl | omega

/-- Homogenization is multiplicative on the steps of the weight filtration: the homogenization of
`p * q` in degree `m + n` is the product of the homogenizations of `p` in degree `m` and of `q` in
degree `n`. -/
theorem weightHomogenization_mul {m n : ℕ} {p q : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hp : p ∈ weightFiltration R w m) (hq : q ∈ weightFiltration R w n) :
    weightHomogenization R w (m + n) (p * q) =
      weightHomogenization R w m p * weightHomogenization R w n q := by
  apply weightReesHom_injective R w
  rw [weightReesHom_weightHomogenization (weightFiltration.instGradedMonoid.mul_mem hp hq),
    map_mul (weightReesHom R w), weightReesHom_weightHomogenization hp,
    weightReesHom_weightHomogenization hq, Polynomial.monomial_mul_monomial]

/-- Setting `t = 1` in a homogenization recovers the polynomial. -/
@[simp]
theorem _root_.MvPolynomial.eval_one_weightHomogenization (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    (weightHomogenization R w n p).eval 1 = p := by
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on' with
  | monomial u r => simp
  | add p q hp hq => simp [hp, hq]

/-- Setting `t = 0` in the homogenization in degree `n` of a polynomial of weight at most `n`
gives its weighted homogeneous component of weight `n`. -/
theorem coeff_zero_weightHomogenization {n : ℕ} {p : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hp : p ∈ weightFiltration R w n) :
    (weightHomogenization R w n p).coeff 0 = weightedHomogeneousComponent w n p := by
  classical
  ext v
  rw [coeff_coeff_weightHomogenization, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent]
  by_cases hv : p.coeff v = 0
  · simp [hv]
  · have := mem_weightFiltration_iff.mp hp v (mem_support_iff.mpr hv)
    split_ifs <;> first | rfl | omega

section CommRing

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- **The special fibre of a homogenized lifted relation.** If `r` is weighted homogeneous of
weight `n` and `Q` has weight less than `n`, then setting `t = 0` in the homogenization of `r - Q`
in degree `n` gives `r`. Setting `t = 1` gives `r - Q` (`eval_one_weightHomogenization`). -/
theorem coeff_zero_weightHomogenization_sub {r Q : MvPolynomial σ R} {n : ℕ}
    (hr : r.IsWeightedHomogeneous w n) (hQ : Q ∈ weightFiltrationLT R w n) :
    (weightHomogenization R w n (r - Q)).coeff 0 = r := by
  have hrQ : r - Q ∈ weightFiltration R w n := by
    rw [← weightFiltrationLT_sup_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule]
    exact sub_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_right ((mem_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R w n r).2 hr))
      (Submodule.mem_sup_left hQ)
  rw [coeff_zero_weightHomogenization hrQ, map_sub,
    weightedHomogeneousComponent_eq_self hr, weightedHomogeneousComponent_eq_zero' (w := w)
      (n := n) (φ := Q) fun x hx ↦ (mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.1 hQ x hx).ne, sub_zero]

end CommRing

end Homogenization

section Substitution

variable {ι : Type*} {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R} {d : ι → ℕ}

/-- The Rees presentation map is `weightReesHom R d`, the substitution `Y i ↦ Y i * t ^ d i`,
followed by the substitution `Y i ↦ c i` in the coefficients. -/
theorem weightReesAeval_eq_comp :
    weightReesAeval c d = (Polynomial.mapAlgHom (aeval c)).comp (weightReesHom R d) := by
  refine Polynomial.algHom_ext' (MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i ↦ ?_) ?_ <;> simp

/-- The Rees presentation map sends the homogenization of `P` in degree `n` to
`aeval c P * tⁿ`. -/
theorem weightReesAeval_weightHomogenization {n : ℕ} {P : MvPolynomial ι R}
    (hP : P ∈ weightFiltration R d n) :
    weightReesAeval c d (weightHomogenization R d n P) = Polynomial.monomial n (aeval c P) := by
  simp [weightReesAeval_eq_comp, weightReesHom_weightHomogenization hP]

variable {w : σ → ℕ}

/-- If each `c i` has weight at most `d i`, the Rees presentation map takes values in the Rees
algebra of the weight filtration. -/
theorem weightReesAeval_mem_weightReesAlgebra (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (f : (MvPolynomial ι R)[X]) : weightReesAeval c d f ∈ weightReesAlgebra R w := by
  have hX : (Polynomial.X : (MvPolynomial σ R)[X]) ∈ weightReesAlgebra R w := by
    simpa using (TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w)).2
  induction f using Polynomial.induction_on with
  | C p =>
    have hp : aeval (fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (c i) * Polynomial.X ^ d i) p ∈
        Algebra.adjoin R (Set.range fun i ↦ Polynomial.C (c i) * Polynomial.X ^ d i) := by
      rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval]
      exact ⟨p, rfl⟩
    rw [weightReesAeval_C]
    refine Algebra.adjoin_le (Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun i ↦ ?_) hp
    rw [Polynomial.C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial, SetLike.mem_coe,
      TauCeti.monomial_mem_coeffSubalgebra_iff]
    exact hc i
  | add f g hf hg => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | monomial n p ih =>
    rw [pow_succ, ← mul_assoc, map_mul, weightReesAeval_X]
    exact mul_mem ih hX

/-- If each `c i` has weight at most `d i`, then substituting the `c i` into a polynomial of weight
at most `n` for the weights `d` gives a polynomial of weight at most `n` for the weights `w`. -/
theorem aeval_mem_weightFiltration (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i)) {n : ℕ}
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} (hP : P ∈ weightFiltration R d n) :
    aeval c P ∈ weightFiltration R w n := by
  have := weightReesAeval_mem_weightReesAlgebra hc (weightHomogenization R d n P)
  rwa [weightReesAeval_weightHomogenization hP, TauCeti.monomial_mem_coeffSubalgebra_iff] at this

/-- **Initial forms of substitutions.** Let each `c i` have weight at most `d i`, with weighted
homogeneous component `g i` of weight `d i`. For `P` of weight at most `n`, the weighted
homogeneous component of weight `n` of `aeval c P` is obtained by substituting the `g i` into the
component of weight `n` of `P`. -/
theorem weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval_of_mem_weightFiltration {g : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (hg : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d i) (c i) = g i) {n : ℕ}
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} (hP : P ∈ weightFiltration R d n) :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent w n (aeval c P) =
      aeval g (weightedHomogeneousComponent d n P) := by
  -- The symbol map of the Rees algebra, after the Rees presentation map, is the substitution of
  -- the `g i` after setting `t = 0`: both are algebra maps, which agree on `Y i` and on `t`.
  set Φ := (weightReesAeval c d).codRestrict (weightReesAlgebra R w)
    (weightReesAeval_mem_weightReesAlgebra hc)
  have key : (weightReesSymbol R w).comp Φ =
      (aeval g).comp ((Polynomial.aeval (0 : MvPolynomial ι R)).restrictScalars R) := by
    refine Polynomial.algHom_ext' (MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i ↦ ?_) ?_
    · have : Φ (Polynomial.C (X i)) = TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.monomial _ (d i) (c i) (hc i) :=
        Subtype.ext (by simp [Φ, Polynomial.C_mul_X_pow_eq_monomial])
      simp [this, hg]
    · have : Φ Polynomial.X = TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.X _ (one_mem_weightFiltration_one R w) :=
        Subtype.ext (by simp [Φ])
      simp [this]
  -- Evaluate both maps at the homogenization of `P` in degree `n`.
  have hΦ : Φ (weightHomogenization R d n P) =
      TauCeti.coeffSubalgebra.monomial _ n (aeval c P) (aeval_mem_weightFiltration hc hP) :=
    Subtype.ext (by simp [Φ, weightReesAeval_weightHomogenization hP])
  have := congr($key (weightHomogenization R d n P))
  simpa only [AlgHom.comp_apply, hΦ, weightReesSymbol_monomial, AlgHom.restrictScalars_apply,
    ← Polynomial.coeff_zero_eq_aeval_zero, coeff_zero_weightHomogenization hP] using this

end Substitution

end TauCeti.MvPolynomial
